export anchor DarkBlueprintStyle:
    number: 294
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Dark blueprint
    idea: The pull request drawn as a technical sheet, white and cyan line work on deep blueprint blue, with a parts list for files, a wiring schematic for checks and a title block for the merge facts.
    base: dark
    palette:
        blueprint: #0a2a52, the page and style sheet ground under a two level grid
        panel: #0c3263, boxes, tabs, counters and the title block
        tint: #123c72, the current tab
        ink: #f2f7ff, text
        muted: #a9c4e8, captions, labels and line numbers
        line: #7fa6d6, secondary rules and dashed leaders
        whiteLine: #e9f2ff, the sheet frame, box outlines and main rules
        cyan: #74e4ff, the accent, primary button, passed checks, added line markers, links and focus
        redline: #ff9c8f, failing check, changes requested, removed line markers and review notes
        addedRow: #0f4470, added diff line ground
        removedRow: #3a3456, removed diff line ground
    type:
        A narrow technical sans, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto
        Condensed, Arial Narrow, system-ui, for text and headings, and a
        system monospace for every label and the diff. Base 15px at 1.5.
        The pull request title is 30px at 600, the repository name 26px at
        600, labels 11px monospace caps tracked 0.14em, the diff 13px
        monospace at 1.7.
    layout:
        The whole screen sits inside a drawing sheet with a 2px white frame,
        an inner 1px rule 8px inside it and faint zone letters A, B and C
        along the top. The header row holds a square B mark with a dashed
        inner square and the app name, the repository name with the
        owner in white and the name in cyan, a boxed Private tag and three
        joined boxed counters for Watch, Star and Fork. Below it the tabs
        are joined outlined boxes, the current one lighter with a cyan
        underline. The body is a main column and a 320px title block.
        Detail A holds the title, the Open tag, the merge sentence and a
        dimension line reading 6 commits, 3 files and the totals. Inside it
        Detail B draws the twelve checks as nodes wired in series with the
        seventh drawn as a dashed octagon that breaks the wire, then a three
        column numbered list. Detail C lists the two reviewers with round
        initial balloons. A parts list table numbers the three files with
        added and removed counts and a totals row. Section D shows the diff
        with the comment as Note 1, a dashed redline box joined to the line
        by a leader with a small circle. The title block is a ruled table of
        cells for assignee, labels, milestone, linked issue and a hatched
        disabled merge button. Every box carries a caption tab cut into its
        top edge. Below 1000px everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px frame padding and gaps, 20px box padding, 16px header gaps.
    density: Medium. Several labelled details are visible at once on the sheet.
    corners: Square everywhere. Only balloons and passed nodes are round.
    borders: 1px white box outlines, a 2px white frame with an inner 1px rule, dashed leaders, and dashed redline borders on anything that blocks the merge.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from line weight and the grid behind.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.5px with square caps and mitred joins. A tick for
        passed, a dashed octagon with a cross for failing, a ringed tick for
        approved, a triangle with a bang for changes requested, a lock on
        the disabled merge, always with the word.
    focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a faint cyan halo.
    tone: Drafting labels in caps, such as Detail A, Parts list, Section D, Title block and Note 1.
